.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"87:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"88:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"89:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe more details you provide, the easier it is for us to reproduce and fix the issue. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T11:18:26.554Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":2.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":171026,"topic_slug":"the-grok-bot-is-not-working","display_username":"system","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/agents","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":-1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/the-grok-bot-is-not-working/171026/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486595,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T15:29:28.562Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report. I can see the screenshot with the cover “Can’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer” and the mention of firewall/proxy and \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, the good news. Your Grok Bot computer on our side is fully healthy, and your bots and data are not affected. The only thing failing is the DNS lookup on your current network. The app can reach our servers, but your network can’t resolve your computer address (a \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e host), so the connection never gets established. This lookup happens on your Mac and your internet connection. That’s why Retry, Reset, and Recover don’t help.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportant: please don’t click Reset, Recover, or Update Computer for now. Each time it rebuilds a computer that is already working fine, and it won’t fix a DNS issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry these 2 steps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSwitch your Mac to a public DNS resolver and fully restart Grok Bot. System Settings → Wi-Fi (or Network) → Details next to your connection → DNS tab → click +, add \u003ccode\u003e1.1.1.1\u003c/code\u003e, then click + again and add \u003ccode\u003e8.8.8.8\u003c/code\u003e, remove the other entries, OK. After that, quit Grok Bot with \u003ccode\u003eCmd+Q\u003c/code\u003e and open it again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a quick check, connect your Mac to a phone hotspot (ideally from a different carrier) and open Grok Bot. If it connects there, it means it’s a DNS issue on your regular network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to verify it yourself, open Terminal and run \u003ccode\u003enslookup test.us9.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003enslookup test.us10.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e. If on your regular network you get “can’t find” or NXDOMAIN, but via hotspot or with \u003ccode\u003e1.1.1.1\u003c/code\u003e in DNS it resolves, that’s the cause.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know how it goes. If neither step helps, tell me which nslookup command failed and we’ll dig deeper.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T15:29:28.562Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":10.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171026,"topic_slug":"the-grok-bot-is-not-working","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/the-grok-bot-is-not-working/171026/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[486349,486350,486595]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1],[3,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"The GROK BOT IS NOT WORKING","id":171026,"title":"The GROK BOT IS NOT WORKING","posts_count":3,"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:18:13.956Z","views":38,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-08T15:29:28.562Z","visible":tru